/-! Complete literal CSR read/write tables and full fixedword FPCSR codecs.
All original counter/clock deltas, saved fields, word masks, inter-core IPI bounds,
unknown-CSR exceptions and arbitrary results are retained. writeCSR uses the
post-write CSR readback for Delta.data2 after recording the CSR address. No
known-CSR/core-bound/success/exception-free premise is introduced.

Literal counter details: high-half reads sign-extend the upper word32 to word64.
High-half writes shift the word32 subtraction by32 before insertion; this
produces zero at that width, clearing the stored delta upper32 and preserving
its lower32. The original counter probe checks this behavior; it must not be
replaced with a widened shift.

The CSR3 write replaces the complete low32-bit FPCSR encoding (including
reserved31..8), although its read exposes only low8. CSR1 replaces only flags4..0,
CSR2 replaces FRM2..0, and each FP control write sets MFS to Dirty and MSD true. -/

